ary_5", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Consonant-Vowel Linking"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When a word ends in a consonant sound, we often move the consonant sound. We only move the consonant when the beginning of the next word starts with a vowel sound."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You push the consonant sound forward and join it to the vowel in the next word."}, {"type": "example", "content": "\u201cSto<span class=\"strong\">p</span>  it\u201d \u2014   Sto <span class=\"strong\">p</span> it "}, {"type": "example", "content": "\u201cI nee<span class=\"strong\">d</span>  it\u201d  \u2014  I nee <span class=\"strong\">d</span> it "}, {"type": "example", "content": "\u201cRea<span class=\"strong\">d</span>  a menu\u201d \u2014 Rea <span class=\"strong\">d</span> a menu"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "help wanted "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a sign asking people to apply for jobs "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I see you have a help-wanted sign in the window."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le02ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use in a store."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Comic Con "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the name of a convention about comics "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Look at this flyer for Comic Con."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le02ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "job application "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a form to complete if you want a job"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Here's the job application form."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le02ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "part-time "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a job you work under 20 hours a week"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Is it a part-time or full-time job?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le02ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to exchange "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to swap, choose another one"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to exchange this comic book."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le02ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to wish "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to hope"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I wish we could go."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le02ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "convention "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a place where large groups of people come together to learn about a subject"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let's go to the Comic Con convention."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le02ob04aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn3le02ob04re1img01.png"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Sh and Ch Sound"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The two sh and ch sounds can be confusing. </br>Here are the differences: </br></br> <span class=\"italic\">Sh</span> has a long, continuous sound.</br> Your tongue just touches the roof of your mouth.</br>Your mouth is slightly closed.</br> Think: \"Shhhh ... the children are sleeping.\" </br></br><span class=\"italic\">Ch</span> has a short, burst of air. </br>Your tongue touches the roof of your mouth.</br>Your mouth opens quickly. </br>Think: \"The train sounds like Choo Choo ... \" "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online and choose a comic book you like."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find a comic book convention in your country."}, {"type": "text", "content": "What is the name of the comic book? Write a sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Where is the convention? Write a sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When is the convention? Write a sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share the information with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read about comic book conventions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write complete statements about comic book conventions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I express the time and location of an event."}]}], "type": "sena"}